# Ford Consul Capri two-door coupe, 1961-1964.
#
# The 335 Consul Capri: the pillarless two-door derivative of the Consul
# Classic on the same 99 in wheelbase, with the low roof falling into a short
# boot and the reverse-rake rear screen. 19,421 built, of which 2,002 were GT.
# It is NOT the 1969-86 Ford Capri.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Consul_Capri
#
# Dimensions 4.337 x 1.659 x 1.372 m, wheelbase 2.515 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation but the car is
# modified with non-standard alloy wheels and a red side stripe; the body and
# glasshouse govern, not the wheels or trim. The front and rear
# three-quarters complete the shape.
#
# Colours: grade (c), the Consul Capri 335 identification sheet. Savoy Black,
# Ermine White, Caribbean Turquoise and Monaco Red. Weights 4, 3, 3, 2,
# total 12, provisional.
#
# Speed 140 km/h. Comfort 55/265, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1962 intro, retires staggered 1979-1982.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-consul-capri.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-consul-capri.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-consul-capri/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear deck is largely inherited from the Classic
# master, and the side-window outline is too angular. The modified alloys and red
# stripe in image 1 were excluded. At 128 px the pillarless two-door cabin and
# rear glass sloping to the boot read as a Consul Capri.


obj=citycar
